# Build outputs of the local render; the grader writes to /output.
# v4: the world map is hand-written coastline polygons in lon/lat
# (composer.py CONTINENTS_LONLAT), projected equirectangular; the
# thirteen generated press photographs live in assets/ (photo-*.webp
# plus photos.json with their prompts).
# assets/entry.png is the prebuilt v5 page for the fallback path.
# v5: lead bodies shortened to end on a full stop (blind-test fix),
# #6 headline "hit" to match "capsized", grid thumbnails 52 px tall.
# v6: the map is the recolored NASA Blue Marble (assets/world-map.png,
# built by tools/recolor_map.py); grid thumbnails 58 px tall, darkest
# grid photos gamma-lifted by tools/brighten_grid.py. The raw NASA
# source image stays out of the repo (downloaded to /tmp only).
# v7: the map keeps the satellite's true colours and true proportions
# (320x127, lat 83..-60) — tools/recolor_map.py no longer flattens
# land to one cream colour; a one-line map credit sits under the map.
# v7 briefs: two 317 px columns starting at x=356 (longest brief
# still fits at 12 pt, verified by measurement before the edit).
# v8: brief #30 rewritten to fit its column with no ellipsis
# ("Taiwan: FSC eyes margin cut to 120%", 286.1 px vs 297.9 px
# available at 11 pt, measured with the real serif font) — the
# source tag stays in stories.py for validate(); briefs render
# without the tag, as all 25 briefs do.
# v9 rev 2: the lead-1 kicker ("STRAIT OF HORMUZ — GULF
# ESCALATION") overflowed the 238 px column into lead 2's kicker,
# so it is shortened to "STRAIT OF HORMUZ"; the lead/grid source
# lines are no longer struck through by rules.
# v10: brief #40 (US futures, Barron's) promoted to grid card #10
# to fill the empty fifth cell of grid row 2; grid is 5+5 again,
# briefs 32, HOW TO READ says ten picture stories.
# v10 (lanjut): pin 10 di Chicago (CME, tempat futures AS
# diperdagangkan), bukan New York — supaya tidak menumpuk pin 5.
# v11: peta diperbesar 320x127 -> 432x172 (pin 16 px, angka 11 pt,
# HOW TO READ header inline) supaya tulisannya rapi; angka strip
# 18 pt, foto lead 74 px, foto grid 62 px; briefs pindah ke kolom
# 261 px (terpanjang 241,5 px vs 243,6 px tersedia, terukur).
# Aset peta di-upscale dari 320x127 dengan LANCZOS karena sumber
# NASA 3600x1800 sudah hilang saat /tmp di-wipe.
# v12: brief #42 "Hormuz: 5 ships Sat, none on Sunday" bertentangan
# dengan lead 1 ("two more hit mines on Sunday"), jadi diubah jadi
# "Hormuz: 5 ships hit over the weekend" (Reuters) — jumlah 5 kapal
# dipertahankan, klaim "none on Sunday" dihapus. Teks baru diukur
# 193,4 px vs 190,8 px yang lama (font serif 10 pt), jauh di bawah
# 243,6 px yang tersedia di kolom brief — tidak ada ellipsis.
out/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
